title: Help
manual:
cite: critic2_2014 critic2_2009

The Help window describes the tool windows of the critic2 graphical interface, one topic per
window. Open a topic from the Help button at the bottom of the window it belongs to, or pick
it from the list in this window. Each topic says what the window does, what its controls mean
(using the same labels as the window) and where the results appear: in the window itself, as
an object in the 3D view, or in the Output console.

The "Open in Manual" button opens the section of the online manual that covers the topic in
the web browser. The manual is the authoritative reference for the behavior of the program and
for the syntax of the command-line keyword that the window corresponds to, named at the top of
the topic.

The References section at the end of a topic lists the papers that describe the method the
window uses. "Open DOI" opens the paper in the browser and "Copy" copies the reference to the
clipboard, so it can be pasted into a manuscript. The keywords of the command-line interface
(the input script language) are documented separately: the Input console has its own Help
button, which describes each keyword.

# Citing critic2

Please cite the two program papers listed under References in any work that uses critic2,
whichever tool or keyword was used. Methods with papers of their own (NCI, XDM, Bader
integration, Hirshfeld partitioning and others) list them in the References of their topic.
